0,Nigerian Fulfulde - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigerian_Fulfulde,"Nigerian Fulfulde, also known as Fulfulde, Fula, or Fulani is a variety of the Fula language spoken by the Fulani people in Nigeria, particularly in the Northern region of Nigeria. It belongs to the West Atlantic branch of the Niger-Congo language family. Phonologically, Nigerian Fulfulde exhibits a system of vowel harmony and a relatively simple consonant inventory, including stops ...","Fulfulde, Nigerian",Niger-Congo
1,Fula language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fula_language,"Fula dialects are also often split into four regions: the Western area, Central area, Niger and Nigeria, and the Eastern area. [6] The dialects are as follows: Western Area Pulaar Pular Central Area Maasina Fulfulde Gorgal Fulflude Borgu Fulfulde Niger and Nigeria Nigerian Fulfulde (also known as Hausa States Fulani) Niger Lettugal Fulfulde ...","Fulfulde, Nigerian",Niger-Congo
2,Nigerian Fulfulde - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigerian_Fulfulde,"Nigerian Fulfulde, also known as Fulfulde, Fula, or Fulani is a variety of the Fula language spoken by the Fulani people in Nigeria, particularly in the Northern region of Nigeria. It belongs to the West Atlantic branch of the Niger-Congo language family. Phonologically, Nigerian Fulfulde exhibits a system of vowel harmony and a relatively simple consonant inventory, including stops ...","Fulfulde, Nigerian",Niger-Congo
